  "question": {
    "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are corresponding points on the ellipse <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and its auxiliary circle respectively. If the normal at <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to the ellipse meets <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> (where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is the origin), then the length of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math> units",
